course: dictionary
lesson: 4877
title: Identification: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Identification is a noun, and it can mean three different things. To find the right one, read the words around it. Context is the clue.
explain: «A PIN, or personal identification number, is a secret 4-digit code for a card.» Here, identification means proof of who you are. The short form is ID, so a personal identification number is a number that proves it is really you.
explain: The word can also mean finding out or naming what something is. Scientists use an identification key to name a leaf or a rock. «Identification of a bird» means working out which bird it is.
explain: Sometimes identification is a feeling. If you read a story and feel like the main character, you feel an identification with them. It means you understand how they feel. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: Identification is a noun, and its short form is ID.
fact: «Identification» can mean proof of who you are, such as a card or passport.
fact: «Identification» can also mean the act of finding out or naming what something is, as in «identification of a bird».
fact: «Identification» can mean a feeling of being like someone and understanding them.
fact: Phrases to know: proof of identification, photo ID, identification key.
exercise: «A PIN, or personal identification number, is a secret 4-digit code for a card.» What does identification mean in this sentence? | *Something that shows who you are | A feeling of sadness | A map of the town | Naming a bird from its song
exercise: Scientists use an identification key to name a leaf. What does identification mean here? | *Finding out or naming what something is | Being like someone and understanding them | A card with your photo on it | Running very fast
exercise: Does identification always mean a card? | Yes, but only for passports | No, it means only a bird | *No, it can also mean naming something or a feeling | Yes, it always means a card
test: The phrase «photo ID» most likely means | Pictures of birds in a book | A feeling of being sad | A lesson in science | *A card with your photo that proves who you are
test: In a story, when police make an identification of a suspect, they are | Going on holiday | Drawing a picture of the suspect | *Finding out or naming who the suspect is | Hiding from the suspect
exam: «She felt a strong identification with the lost girl in the book.» What does identification mean here? | Proof of who she is, on a card | *Feeling like the girl and understanding how she feels | A map of the town where the girl lives | Naming the girl's bird
